#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:1
msgid "prql-dotnet"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:3
msgid "`prql-net` offers PRQL bindings for .NET as a `net10.0` library."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:5
msgid ""
"It provides the static `PrqlCompiler` class, whose `Compile`, `PrqlToPl`, "
"`PlToRq` and `RqToSql` methods each return a `Result` carrying the "
"compiler's `Output` string and any `Messages`."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:9
msgid ""
"It's still at an early stage, and isn't published to NuGet. Contributions "
"are welcome."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:12
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:14
msgid ""
"Make sure that `libprqlc_c.so` (Linux), `libprqlc_c.dylib` (macOS) or "
"`libprqlc_c.dll` (Windows) is in the project's `bin` directory together with "
"`PrqlCompiler.dll` and the rest of the project's compiled files. I.e. "
"`{your_project}/bin/Debug/net10.0/`."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:19
msgid "The `libprqlc_c` library gets dynamically imported at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:21
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/dotnet.md:23
msgid ""
"```csharp\n"
"using Prql.Compiler;\n"
"\n"
"var options = new PrqlCompilerOptions\n"
"{\n"
"    Format = false,\n"
"    SignatureComment = false,\n"
"};\n"
"var result = PrqlCompiler.Compile(\"from employees\", options);\n"
"Console.WriteLine(result.Output);\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

